<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sahibdin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1628">1628</a>–<a href="/years/1655">1655</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sahibdin was a Muslim painter at the court of Mewar in the mid-seventeenth century and the leading artist of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> school under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a> Jagat Singh I. His works include a Ragamala series of 1628 and illustrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> of the Bhagavata Purana and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramayana">Ramayana</a>, among them parts of the great Mewar Ramayana of the 1650s, whose bright colours and crowded narrative scenes defined classic Mewar painting.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sahibdin.jpg" alt="Sahibdin" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sahibdin (fl. 17th century) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishna_and_Radha_in_a_Bower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
